      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ninilchik%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Russian colonists from Kodiak Island founded Ninilchik in 1847, two decades before the U.S. bought Alaska.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ninilchik%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Ninilchik boasts a Russian Orthodox church and panoramic views of Cook Inlet volcanoes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ninilchik%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Just south of Ninilchik lies Deep Creek State Recreation Area, featuring a beach campground and boat launching.",
